// LEARNER VERSION: runs on embedded SYNTHETIC rows (no ingestion needed). Generated by scripts/build_datatable_queries.py - do not edit by hand.
// Name: Successful sign-ins from a suspect IP
// Description: Lists which accounts a suspect IP signed in to successfully, to find the accounts that need priority review.
// MITRE: T1078.004 (Valid Accounts: Cloud Accounts) - possible, not proven by this query alone
// Tables: SigninLogs
// Status: SIMULATED - logic verified offline on synthetic data; NOT run in a live Microsoft Sentinel workspace
// Assumptions: suspectIP comes from the previous triage step (a documentation-range IP in this lab).
// Limitations: A successful sign-in is not proof of compromise; it does not show MFA, Conditional Access outcome or what the session did afterwards.
